==Trivia==
* Palmer is the only Trainer to have an animated battle sprite in {{game|Platinum}} and {{game|HeartGold and SoulSilver|s}}; in his appearance at the end of the battle, his hair and coattails blow in the "wind".
** Also, his quotes said to the player differ between Diamond, Pearl, and Platinum, and HeartGold and SoulSilver, with references to his home in Sinnoh, even including his son, removed.
* Palmer's [[List of battle music themes|battle music]] in {{game|Diamond and Pearl|s}} and {{g|Brilliant Diamond and Shining Pearl}} is the same as [[Cynthia]]'s battle theme. In Platinum, it changes to match the other four [[Frontier Brain]]s.
** Coincidentally, he was battling {{an|Cynthia}} herself in his first {{pkmn|animated series}}-related appearance, in the cameo at the beginning of [[M12|the twelfth movie]]. They both have a {{p|Milotic}} in the {{pkmn|games}}.
* Palmer's coat has the kanji {{tt|王|おう}} ''ō'', meaning "king", on the back.
* Palmer is the only [[Sinnoh]]/[[Johto]] Frontier Brain to:
** Have a known hometown.
** Appear in a {{pkmn|movie}}, having appeared in both ''[[M12|Arceus and the Jewel of Life]]'' and ''[[M13|Zoroark: Master of Illusions]]''.
** Appear in the animated series.
** Appear in Pokémon Brilliant Diamond and Shining Pearl.
** Have not been defeated by {{adv|Platinum}} in [[Pokémon Adventures]].
* Palmer shares the trait of being the {{tc|Tower Tycoon}} of his region with [[Anabel]].

